* Reference 1.4: invisible characters are ignored between lexical units and act
* as separators, and lexical units may follow one another without them -- which
* is why `s1s2s3` is `s1 s2 s3`. The dotted form is not self-delimiting, so the
* same juxtaposition is a syntax error: the reference states it outright with
* `s.1s.2s.3`, and this fixture is that example.
$ENTRY Go {
  s.1s.2s.3 = ;
}
